From eed1303a40c0a8f705a68c79a699ad2770c0edd7 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: webby <webby@localhost>
Date: Wed, 25 Nov 2026 17:35:30 +0800
Subject: [PATCH 6/8] WC compositor: layers that show images handed over by
 WebCore

Adds WCPlatformLayerImage, a platform layer whose contents are images
supplied one at a time, such as the frames of a video. GraphicsLayerWC sends
the current image with the layer update as a shareable bitmap, and WCScene
shows it as a texture of its own that the compositor scales.

Without this a video is painted into the tiles of the page around it. Tiles
are rasterized on the CPU, so the cost grows with the painted area: a 1080p
video reached 15 frames a second on screen in a window and 11 in fullscreen.
